WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:04.665
Looking for something specific? Ask your pack in plain words —

00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:07.592
"lines with Paris and at least 14 days off" —

00:00:07.592 --> 00:00:14.030
and it hands back the pack's own lines that match, in your order, with the figures behind each one.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:22.157
Sort by almost anything: credit, days off, weekends, hub turns, the body-clock score — around ninety ways.

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:26.711
Sorting is only for looking; your bid still follows your ranking.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:34.110
Filters narrow the list: days off, credit, report times, deadheads, layover cities.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:41.146
If you commute, it can keep only the lines you can actually commute to and from on real airline flights.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:54.153
To weigh two lines against each other, press "Compare" on each.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:01:00.111
You get them side by side — days off, credit, body clock, and both months on the calendar.

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:09.194
And if you know the line number, press Command-K —

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.920
Control-K on Windows — and type it to jump straight there.

